INSERT INTO fact (id,subject_id,text,provenance_class,trust_class,source_url,source_host,source_date,observed_at,composed_from,search_first_page,via_edge_type,via_person_id,run_id) VALUES

-- ── Hacker News. HANDLE IS `emmett`. His single richest open archive ──────────
('f_shear_001','m_shear','His Hacker News profile "about", verbatim and current: "Founder and CEO of Softmax. Softmax is building massively multiplayer benchmarks for coding agents to train social intelligence. Previously very interim CEO of OpenAI, YC Partner, and founder and CEO of Twitch. Email me at emmett@softmax.com." Account created 2007-02-19, karma 4,858.','self_published','subject_authored','https://hacker-news.firebaseio.com/v0/user/emmett.json','hacker-news.firebaseio.com','2026-09-03','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

('f_shear_002','m_shear','Posted the Softmax job ad himself to Ask HN: Who is hiring? (March 2026) — his most recent HN item, 2026-03-02: "THE MOST IMPORTANT UNSOLVED PROBLEM IN AI IS THE MOST POWERFUL OF ALL CAPABILITIES: ALIGNMENT. Hi, I''m Emmett. You may know me as the founder of Twitch (YC S05), and as the (extremely) interim CEO of OpenAI. I believe the question of how AI systems learn to understand themselves and others is one of the most consequential technical problems of our time. If we get it right, the agents we build today will become our friends and collaborators tomorrow... Softmax is building large-scale multi-agent, multi-policy environments that will benchmark AI agents — both our own and others — on their capacity for theory of mind, adaptive goal setting, and teamwork... The work is unusually hard. The problems are ambiguous and challenging. High autonomy, high expectations. You''ll work directly with me and the rest of our small but mighty team."','self_published','subject_authored','https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47219766','news.ycombinator.com','2026-03-02','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

('f_shear_003','m_shear','On Y Combinator''s first house going up for sale, 2010-10-22, in his own words: "This is where we wrote a good deal of the code for Kiko, and where Steve wrote a lot of Reddit. It makes me nostalgic for our 2005 YC batch, and sad to see it go on the market. I hope whoever buys it puts it to good use." The "Steve" is Steve Huffman: the Summer 2005 batch tie is Kiko <-> Reddit, NOT Twitch <-> Reddit — Twitch''s own YC batch is Winter 2007, which is Justin.tv''s.','self_published','subject_authored','https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=1821879','news.ycombinator.com','2010-10-22','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

('f_shear_004','m_shear','How he got into that batch at all, told against himself four days earlier, 2010-10-18: "Justin and I applied for Kiko Calendar (YC S05) just before the deadline. We only found out about 2 days before that it even existed. I think we convinced the airbnb guys to apply for YC on the day of the deadline."','self_published','subject_authored','https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=1804706','news.ycombinator.com','2010-10-18','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

('f_shear_005','m_shear','Correcting the record on who founded Reddit, 2011-06-17: "Jedberg was not on the founding team of Reddit. The founding team of reddit was Steve Huffman (spez) and Alexis Ohanian (kn0thing). Jedberg was their first hire after acquisition, though they''d acquired two other team members via merger (Chris Slowe and Aaron Swartz) prior to that." He is the only member of the ten who writes Huffman''s name unprompted.','self_published','subject_authored','https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=2666830','news.ycombinator.com','2011-06-17','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

('f_shear_006','m_shear','Shape of the HN archive: Algolia returns 927 items under author_emmett, 2007-02-19 to 2026-03-02, of which 51 are submissions and 876 comments; the peak is 2008 (249 items) and output falls away after 2017 (14, then 8, 6, 5, 3, 1, 1). Note the two counters disagree: the Firebase user object lists 1,167 ids in `submitted` against Algolia''s 927 — the gap is dead/deleted items Algolia does not index. Karma 4,858.','self_published','subject_authored','https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/search_by_date?tags=author_emmett&hitsPerPage=1000','hn.algolia.com','2026-09-03','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

-- ── softmax.com. robots.txt allows all but /api/observatory/v2/coworlds/replays/ ──
('f_shear_007','m_shear','His company blog carries six pieces and only two are his: "Rheomode: When Language Flows Like Reality" and "The Frame-Dependent Mind: On Reality''s Stubborn Refusal To Be One Thing", both bylined "Emmett Shear and Sonnet 3.7" (the Rheomode byline adds "based on the work of David Bohm"), both April 2025. The other four are bylined "Softmax Team" (March-April 2025) or "Yatharth Agarwal" (April 2026). No RSS exists anywhere on the domain; sitemap.xml is the only machine-readable index.','self_published','subject_authored','https://softmax.com/blog','softmax.com','2026-04-30','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

('f_shear_008','m_shear','From "Rheomode", his own opening: "I first encountered David Bohm''s Rheomode while trying to describe a strange pattern in deep learning. The model wasn''t ''making mistakes'' - rather, ''mistaking happened.'' The difference feels subtle but profound. In one framing, an entity (the model) performs an action (making) on an object (mistakes). In the other, a process (mistaking) simply occurs." He goes on: "As a physicist-turned-philosopher, Bohm created Rheomode to address what he saw as a critical limitation in our thinking: our tendency to fragment holistic processes into discrete objects."','self_published','subject_authored','https://softmax.com/blog/rheomode','softmax.com','2025-04-19','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

('f_shear_009','m_shear','From "The Frame-Dependent Mind", the apple: "If I hold one up and ask, ''What is this?'', you might reasonably say ''an apple.'' But this seemingly trivial act of identification conceals something profound: a frame has just been imposed on reality... A botanist might point out that the ''apple'' is actually a swollen stem... A physicist sees not an apple but a temporary configuration of atoms... None of these perspectives is fundamentally wrong. Equally importantly, none is fundamentally right."','self_published','subject_authored','https://softmax.com/blog/the-frame-dependent-mind','softmax.com','2025-04-18','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

('f_shear_010','m_shear','His own card on the Softmax team page, verbatim: "Emmett Shear — CEO & Founder. Partner at YC, founder and CEO of Twitch, and extremely interim CEO at OpenAI. Independent researcher in alignment and agency before cofounding Softmax." The card links exactly two accounts, x.com/eshear and linkedin.com/in/emmettshear — which is how the LinkedIn slug was established rather than guessed.','self_published','subject_authored','https://softmax.com/team','softmax.com','2026-09-03','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

('f_shear_011','m_shear','Softmax states its own thesis on the same page: "We''re a small team building the science of organic alignment: the claim that the kinds of agents that stay aligned with us are the kinds that stay aligned with each other." It lists two Founders (Shear, David Bloomin) and two Board members: Adam Goldstein — "Board Member and Founder Emeritus. Cofounded Hipmunk before joining Michael Levin''s lab at Tufts to research cell signaling, bioelectricity, and basal cognition. Cofounded Softmax and brought the organic alignment thesis into the company''s multi-agent research" — and David Langer of Lionheart Ventures.','on_record','publisher','https://softmax.com/team','softmax.com','2026-09-03','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

('f_shear_012','m_shear','From "Reimagining Alignment", the Softmax Team statement of the idea he built the company on: "All alignment between individuals is a matter of shared fundamental goals. Organic alignment occurs when these individuals find themselves in groups with mutual interdependence, and take on an overarching shared goal of the healthy development and flourishing of the group as a whole... We call it organic alignment because it is the form of alignment that evolution has learned most often for aligning living things. One of the best examples is multicellularity... The ''we'' of the cells becomes an ''I''."','on_record','publisher','https://softmax.com/blog/reimagining-alignment','softmax.com','2025-03-28','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

-- ── edbs.media — his personal site, NOT on the allow-list, found via his own LinkedIn post ──
('f_shear_013','m_shear','He keeps a personal site nobody has catalogued: edbs.media, titled "Welcome to the Educational Database System", styled as a database console with a nav of four "Query:" links. The whole homepage is a first-person index: "I''m the CEO of Softmax, a research company dedicated to scaling organic alignment (2025-present) / I gave a talk on the the future of trust and nature evidence in the era of AI (2024) / I have a Twitter that some people like; check the higlights for the best content (mostly 2020-present) / Technology is intrinsically corrosive and atomizing unless you fight it: Welcome to my TED TALK (2019) / How To Run A User Interview, A Lecture (2015) / I made Twitch (2010) / I co-wrote a paper about how electronic voting machines are a bad idea (2004)". Footer: "EDBS v1.0.0 | Status: Operational". This is the site the eshear.com parking page and the dead emmettshear.com apex have been standing in for.','self_published','subject_authored','https://www.edbs.media/','edbs.media','2026-09-03','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

('f_shear_014','m_shear','From "Im/mortality" on that site — the essay he announced on LinkedIn as "a blog post on Im/mortality": "There''s a particular kind of existential vertigo that comes from realizing you''re not your atoms... Ship of Theseus paradox? Sure, but more importantly: you''re not the ship. You''re the pattern that the ship is in." And the thesis: "you are not your parts — you''re the arrangement, the dance, the information structure that those parts happen to embody at this particular moment... it''s actually the key to understanding something profound about what you are, why you age, and why sexual reproduction isn''t just a bizarre cosmic accident but something closer to a mathematical necessity."','self_published','subject_authored','https://www.edbs.media/aging','edbs.media','2026-09-03','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

('f_shear_015','m_shear','The same site carries his standing book-recommendation database, organised under his own headings: "Sci-fi about Identity" (Greg Egan''s Axiomatic, Hannu Rajaniemi''s Quantum Thief trilogy), "Sci-Fi To Understand The Future", "Non-fiction about The Nature Of The Universe" (Gordon''s The New Science Of Strong Materials, Denis Noble''s Dance to the Tune of Life, Aaronson''s Quantum Computing Since Democritus), "Romantic Fantasy" (Jonathan Strange & Mr Norrell, Jemisin, Novik), "The New Metaphysics" (Ken Wilber, Deutsch''s The Fabric of Reality, Friston''s Active Inference, Pirsig), "Introspection and Extrospection", "Education", "Material History", "Institutional Formation" (two James C. Scott titles), "Actually New Ideas For Governance", "Intellectual Scenes". About 60 titles in all.','self_published','subject_authored','https://www.edbs.media/books','edbs.media','2026-09-03','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

('f_shear_016','m_shear','And a 2024 reading log with a paragraph of his own commentary per book. On Stafford Beer: "Part of my ''understanding reasoning systems'' arc. Stafford Beer was a management school professor who invented a cybernetic approach to organizations he called Syntegrity. He convinced the president of Chile, Allende, to try implementing it before Allende was assassinated. Some really prescient predictions about how the internet would wind up impacting our collective politics and thinking. Worth reading." On Donald Hoffman''s The Case Against Reality: "I wanted to yell at the book ''I GET IT'' like 5 times a chapter, but I still think I got something out of reading it." On MacIntyre''s After Virtue: "Part of my ''figure out how morality works'' reading kick... In buddhist terminology I''d say he''s exploring how morality is empty, which seems right." He also names the reading he did to prepare a talk — Poovey''s A History of the Modern Fact, MacCormack''s The Spirit of Traditional Chinese Law, Blair''s Too Much To Know.','self_published','subject_authored','https://www.edbs.media/books2024','edbs.media','2026-09-03','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

('f_shear_017','m_shear','The 2004 paper his own site points to: "Tiny Systematic Vote Manipulations Can Swing Elections", Yale University Department of Computer Science technical report YALEU/DCS/TR-1285, April 2004, by Anthony Di Franco, Andrew Petro, Vladimir Vladimirov and Emmett Shear. Abstract: "We examine the effects of a type of electoral fraud easily perpetrated by someone with access to the system software for a direct-recording electronic voting system... We conclude that changing only a single vote per electronic voting machine can change the outcome of the election." The footnote: "The authors are undergraduates at Yale University." (cpsc.yale.edu 403s every automated client; read via Wayback.)','on_record','publisher','http://web.archive.org/web/20230610081136/https://cpsc.yale.edu/sites/default/files/files/tr1285.pdf','cpsc.yale.edu','2004-04-01','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

-- ── Wikipedia wikitext ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
('f_shear_018','m_shear','Born 1983, grew up in Seattle, attended the Evergreen School for Gifted Children and the Transition School at the University of Washington, then read computer science at Yale and graduated in 2005 — the same year and the same city as YC''s first batch. He attended Yale with his eventual Twitch co-founders Justin Kan and Michael Seibel.','on_record','publisher','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emmett_Shear','en.wikipedia.org','2026-09-03','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

('f_shear_019','m_shear','He met Justin Kan at the Evergreen School at age eight, "bonded by their accelerated math classes and playing Magic: The Gathering" — the co-founder relationship predates the company by roughly seventeen years.','on_record','publisher','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emmett_Shear','en.wikipedia.org','2026-09-03','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

('f_shear_020','m_shear','"Shear and Justin Kan were part of Y Combinator''s first class in 2005. As part of Y Combinator, the two built a calendar application called Kiko, which they eventually sold on eBay for around $250,000 after Google Calendar was introduced."','on_record','publisher','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emmett_Shear','en.wikipedia.org','2026-09-03','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

('f_shear_021','m_shear','Justin.tv launched March 2007 with Shear, Justin Kan, Michael Seibel and Kyle Vogt. The gaming spin-off was named in June 2011; Shear became CEO on 2011-08-29 and stayed through the 2014 rebrand to Twitch, Amazon''s $970m acquisition on 2014-08-25, and until March 2023, when he announced he was resigning and Daniel J. Clancy would take over. He was appointed a part-time partner at Y Combinator in June 2011.','on_record','publisher','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emmett_Shear','en.wikipedia.org','2026-09-03','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

('f_shear_022','m_shear','"In November 2023, he was briefly the interim CEO of OpenAI" — appointed after Sam Altman''s removal, and on November 21 an agreement was reached to reinstate Altman. He describes the same episode himself as "(extremely) interim" and "very interim".','on_record','publisher','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emmett_Shear','en.wikipedia.org','2026-09-03','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

('f_shear_023','m_shear','"In March 2025, Shear co-founded Softmax, a startup focused on AI alignment, alongside Adam Goldstein and David Bloomin." Goldstein is the Hipmunk co-founder; Hipmunk''s other co-founder is Steve Huffman. That is the SECOND bridge from Shear to Huffman, twenty years after the first.','on_record','publisher','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emmett_Shear','en.wikipedia.org','2026-09-03','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

('f_shear_024','m_shear','"In March 2020, during the COVID-19 pandemic, via Twitch, Shear donated the initial US$1 million to start SF New Deal, a non-profit organization which ordered meals from San Francisco eateries and delivered them to people in need. The organization was started by his Yale college classmate Leonore Estrada, who owned the Three Babes Bakeshop in San Francisco''s Bayview neighborhood."','on_record','publisher','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emmett_Shear','en.wikipedia.org','2026-09-03','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

-- ── GitHub ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
('f_shear_025','m_shear','GitHub account `eshear`: name field "Emmett Shear", location "San Francisco, CA", 9 public repos, 0 gists, 48 followers, following 2, joined 2009-02-04, profile last updated 2026-05-24. No bio and no blog field, so the name field is the identity signal. github.com/emmettshear is 404.','self_published','subject_authored','https://api.github.com/users/eshear','api.github.com','2026-09-03','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

('f_shear_026','m_shear','What is actually in those nine repos is a picture of the last twelve months, not of 2009: `autoquine` (Python, created 2025-12-09, last pushed 2026-02-25), `softmax-universe` ("Game service ontology and admin dashboard", 2026-04-07), `tweetgrabber` (Python, 2025-04-25), plus forks of `metta` — "A reinforcement learning codebase focusing on the emergence of cooperation and alignment", Softmax''s own — `pong-wars` (pushed 2026-04-01), `noteswiki` and, from another era entirely, `xmpp4r-simple` (2010) and `homebrew-versions` (2012, the package manager, not the venture firm).','self_published','subject_authored','https://api.github.com/users/eshear/repos?per_page=100','api.github.com','2026-09-03','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

