('f_shear_045','m_shear','LinkedIn, logged-out archived copy of 2026-05-21: og:title "Emmett Shear - San Francisco, California, United States | Professional Profile | LinkedIn", "Location: San Francisco · 500+ connections", 6K followers. The archived page also renders a Languages section listing Chinese, and no Experience or Education section at all — the logged-out surface simply does not carry his career history.','self_published','subject_authored','http://web.archive.org/web/20260521164402/https://www.linkedin.com/in/emmettshear','linkedin.com','2026-05-21','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

('f_shear_046','m_shear','LinkedIn read live on the operator''s logged-in Chrome, read-only: headline "Researching organic alignment" — NOT "CEO of Softmax". Location San Francisco, California, United States; current company Softmax; education Yale University; 500+ connections; 5,879 followers. The headline is the one place in the set where he describes himself by what he is doing rather than what he runs.','self_published','subject_authored','https://www.linkedin.com/in/emmettshear/','linkedin.com','2026-09-04','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

('f_shear_047','m_shear','His own LinkedIn post, about eleven months old: "Working on Softmax has inspired me to explore the nature of living systems. I recently wrote a blog post on Im/mortality, which delves into these ideas. You can read it here: https://lnkd.in/gJEnvTuj." The link card on the post reads "Im/mortality — edbs.media". This is the link that establishes edbs.media as his: a page already confirmed as his, pointing at it.','self_published','subject_authored','https://www.linkedin.com/in/emmettshear/','linkedin.com','2025-10-04','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

('f_shear_048','m_shear','Two years ago on the same account, unanswered: "If I start posting on linkedin like it''s Twitter, will I get engagement? Using linkedin to actually share ideas feels subversive somehow, like publishing real philosophy in a corporate newsletter." It drew 123 reactions and 19 comments, and he then posted four more times in two years.','self_published','subject_authored','https://www.linkedin.com/in/emmettshear/','linkedin.com','2024-09-04','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

('f_shear_049','m_shear','The only thing he has reposted on LinkedIn in two years is Michael Seibel leaving Y Combinator: "Today after 12+ years at Y Combinator I''ll be transitioning to Partner Emeritus... The next adventure I''m excited to pursue (after taking the summer to relax) is how I can help government better serve citizens with technology... Thank you to @ycombinator @paulg and @jesslivingston for changing my life." Shear both liked and reposted it.','self_published','subject_authored','https://www.linkedin.com/in/emmettshear/','linkedin.com','2025-09-04','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

('f_shear_050','m_shear','The archived profile carries exactly one recommendation, attributed to Justin Kan: "Emmett is a great co-founder: works hard, doesn''t complain, and the smartest guy I know." Written by someone other than the subject on a surface he controls acceptance of — recorded as third-party-open, so it is countable and traversable but never rendered.','third_party','third_party_open','http://web.archive.org/web/20260521164402/https://www.linkedin.com/in/emmettshear','linkedin.com','2026-05-21','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

