('f_shear_053','m_shear','eshear.substack.com exists, is titled "Emmett''s Substack", describes itself as "My personal Substack", and contains exactly one post in its entire life: "Coming soon", 2023-10-17, zero reactions, zero restacks. A 200 and a valid feed with one placeholder item in it.','self_published','subject_authored','https://eshear.substack.com/api/v1/archive?sort=new&limit=50','eshear.substack.com','2023-10-17','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

('f_shear_054','m_shear','Three recorded talks, each linked from his own site and each carrying his name in the video title on a third-party channel — so the attribution does not rest on the channel: TED, "What streaming means for the future of entertainment | Emmett Shear" (his site dates it 2019, and glosses it "Technology is intrinsically corrosive and atomizing unless you fight it"); YC Root Access, "Lecture 16 - How to Run a User Interview (Emmett Shear)" (2015); Manifold Markets, "The Future of Trust and Evidence, in the Age of AI by Emmett Shear" (2024). He names the last one as the talk he did the Poovey / MacCormack / Blair reading for.','on_record','publisher','https://www.edbs.media/','edbs.media','2026-09-03','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z',NULL,0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

