-- ── The label correction, and the absence evidence ───────────────────────────
('f_shear_056','m_shear','The supplied label "Twitch" is STALE and the correction is on four independent surfaces measured the same day: x.com/eshear og:description "CEO of Softmax: Massively Multiplayer Learning Environments"; his HN about, "Founder and CEO of Softmax"; softmax.com/team, "CEO & Founder"; instagram.com/emmettshear, "CEO of Softmax". He left Twitch in March 2023. A host who opens with "so, Twitch..." is three and a half years out of date, and keying the ingest on Twitch also loses the strongest edge in his profile, because the Y Combinator tie to Steve Huffman is Kiko <-> Reddit in Summer 2005, not Twitch <-> Reddit — Twitch''s YC page says Winter 2007, which is Justin.tv''s batch.','inferred','subject_authored','https://x.com/eshear','x.com','2026-09-03','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z','["f_shear_001","f_shear_003","f_shear_010","f_shear_021","f_shear_028","f_shear_051"]',0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

('f_shear_057','m_shear','MEASURED ABSENCE, corpus named. All 927 indexed Hacker News items under author_emmett (2007-02-19 to 2026-03-02) were full-text searched for each of the other nine members by surname, first name, firm and product. Zero occurrences of Feld, Kopelman, Tavel, Walk, Ries, Qureshi or Perkins in any form — every apparent hit was a common noun ("benchmark", "first round of funding") or an unrelated Josh. Fred Wilson occurs exactly twice, 2008-10-28 and 2011-09-25, and BOTH are HN story titles of threads Shear commented in ("Fred Wilson''s Survival Matrix"; "Moneyball for startups? PG, Fred Wilson, Chris Dixon discuss") — Shear never writes the name himself, so this is not a citation. Steve Huffman is the only member he names, twice, unprompted.','inferred','subject_authored','https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/search_by_date?tags=author_emmett&hitsPerPage=1000','hn.algolia.com','2026-09-03','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z','["f_shear_003","f_shear_005","f_shear_006"]',1,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

('f_shear_058','m_shear','Career start: he graduated Yale in 2005 and was in Y Combinator''s first batch the same summer, which puts the start of his working life in the 2000s and fixes person.career_start_decade at ''2000s''. The 2004 Yale technical report predates even that by a year, but as an undergraduate publication it is not a career start.','inferred','publisher','https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emmett_Shear','en.wikipedia.org','2026-09-03','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z','["f_shear_017","f_shear_018","f_shear_020"]',0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

('f_shear_059','m_shear','Shear and Steve Huffman were in the same Y Combinator batch, Summer 2005, in the same house — Shear building Kiko, Huffman building Reddit. The relationship is symmetric as a shared organisation and ASYMMETRIC as citation: Shear writes about Huffman on his own initiative twice (2010, 2011); no reciprocal citation was looked for in this run and none is asserted.','inferred','subject_authored','https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=1821879','news.ycombinator.com','2010-10-22','2026-09-04T01:45:00Z','["f_shear_003","f_shear_004","f_shear_005","f_shear_020"]',0,NULL,NULL,'run_ingest_shear_20260903'),

